00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.389
- This is a cute dress too.

00:00:01.389 --> 00:00:02.380
- Thank you, thank you.

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.920
I actually busted the belt,

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.610
so we just had to sew
it in the car, you know.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:09.360
But we're here, we're doing it, thank you.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.710
- Meet Tinashe, meet Jeff.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.280
- Hi guys.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.860
- So Jeff's family named him Chex Mix.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.180
So how did you get the name Tinx?

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.970
- So when I was younger, I
actually wasn't that confident.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.530
And so I watched this movie

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.300
and there was a character in this movie

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.040
called All I Wanna Do,
called Tinker Parker.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.190
And she was like the coolest girl.

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:28.220
And I told my friends,

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.890
I was like, guys I have an alter ego now,

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:32.000
her name is Tinker Parker.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.920
And when I'm her, I'm confident
and I'm cool and whatever.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.970
And slowly I just started
to become more confident

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.620
and slowly they just started
to call me Tinker Parker

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.200
then Tinker then Tinx.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.340
So I've been called Tinx
for like 20 years now.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.690
- That's cute.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.810
Its like my Sasha Fierce moment, you know?

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:48.643
- Yeah.

00:00:48.643 --> 00:00:51.000
- We all need a nickname and alter ego.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.833
- It is funny.

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:53.340
I don't know if y'all feel
this when you're on stage

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.620
but I do feel like different

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.950
and I do feel more bold and confident.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.170
Do you feel like that
when you're on stage?

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:59.320
- Absolutely, there's
like this part of me,

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.190
I call her Nashe,

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:02.493
I just drop like the
first syllable of my name.

00:01:02.493 --> 00:01:04.740
And like she this like super confident.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.650
It's weird cause it lives
inside of you already.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.650
But it gives the opportunity
to feel like you can kind of--

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:10.483
- Absolutely.

00:01:10.483 --> 00:01:11.580
- Step into that, you know?

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:12.413
- Yeah.
- [Tinashe] So much.

00:01:12.413 --> 00:01:13.990
- Do you feel like that
on stage more confident?

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.670
- Yeah, I just feel like
I'm talking to my friends

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.410
so I look forward to it.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:19.910
- Oh, I think that's why
people love you though too,

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:21.300
cause you're so relatable in that sense.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.133
It's conversational.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:23.190
- [Jeff] Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.223
Everybody loves everybody here.

